{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"22854","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/22854","key":"MC-277889","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"27/Oct/24 9:09 PM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>According to the Minecraft Wiki, an Iron Golem is detected by a Villager when it is within 16 blocks of the villager.</p>\n\n<p>I have recently discovered that the Iron Golem Detection range for villager is far greater than that in <em>1.21.2</em> and <em>1.21.3</em>, while it works as intended in <em>1.21.1</em>. I assume it must be a bug as I have not seen any patch notes regarding the Iron Golem detection range.</p>\n\n<p>The detection range in <em>1.21.2</em> and <em>1.21.3</em> is about 45 blocks instead of 16. This can easily be tested by placing three Villagers with a bed each and a Zombie to scare, and an Iron Golem more than 16 but less than about 45 blocks away from the Villagers - in every version up to <em>1.21.1</em> (including <em>1.21.1</em>), the Villagers will spawn a new Iron Golem if there is any space for it. In <em>1.21.2</em> and upwards, the Villagers won't be able to spawn a new Iron Golem. Using gnembon's Carpet mod, you can also see the Villager's \"Iron Golem Seen\" counter go back to 600 ticks every 10 seconds after counting down.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howtoreproduce%3A\"></a>How to reproduce:</h3>\n<p>Attached is a world in 1.21.1 containing an iron farm, an iron golem placed 18 blocks away from the villagers, and a repeating command block to check the last time a villager detected an iron golem around.</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open the attached world (<span class=\"nobr\"><a href=\"/rest/api/3/attachment/content/40408\" title=\"MC-277889.zip attached to MC-277889\" data-attachment-type=\"file\" data-attachment-name=\"MC-277889.zip\" data-media-services-type=\"file\" data-media-services-id=\"3869232e-2204-4f93-9a6b-506424a2cc52\" rel=\"noreferrer\">MC-277889.zip<sup><img class=\"rendericon\" src=\"/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif\" height=\"7\" width=\"7\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"></sup></a></span>) in 1.21.1.</li>\n\t<li>Periodically check the repeating command block's output until there is no number in the output, at which point the villagers will try to spawn a golem.</li>\n\t<li>Wait until the villagers spawn a golem.<br>\n→ <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/check.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"> The villagers successfully spawn a golem.</li>\n\t<li>Upgrade the world to 1.21.2 or higher.</li>\n\t<li>Periodically check the repeating command block's output.<br>\n→ <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/error.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"> The output never reaches 0, which means the villagers now detect the iron golem that is 18 blocks away, so they will never spawn a golem.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"Expectedresult%3A\"></a>Expected result:</h3>\n<p>The villagers' iron golem detection range would not change when upgrading to a newer version.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Observedresult%3A\"></a>Observed result:</h3>\n<p>The villagers' iron golem detection range changes from <span class=\"error\">[0, 16]</span> to <span class=\"error\">[16, ~45]</span> when upgrading to a newer version.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"31/Oct/24 5:02 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/40407","id":"40407","filename":"2024-10-31_00-17-07_New World (1).zip","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d70168bc4d0c82762f0a18f8b5637505?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FM-5.png"},"displayName":"migrated","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Los_Angeles","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"30/Oct/24 4:19 PM","size":"1.41 MB","mimeType":"application/zip","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/40407"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/40408","id":"40408","filename":"MC-277889.zip","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5ec8dd4db199aa0c1306447c/7698f7c4-2508-4ce5-a207-0b2918018f22/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5ec8dd4db199aa0c1306447c/7698f7c4-2508-4ce5-a207-0b2918018f22/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5ec8dd4db199aa0c1306447c/7698f7c4-2508-4ce5-a207-0b2918018f22/16","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5ec8dd4db199aa0c1306447c/7698f7c4-2508-4ce5-a207-0b2918018f22/32"},"displayName":"[Mod] ManosSef","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Athens","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"31/Oct/24 9:46 AM","size":"987 kB","mimeType":"application/zip","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/40408"}],"versions":null,"resolutiondate":"29/Nov/24 7:52 AM","issuelinks":null,"updated":"20/Aug/26 4:36 AM","status":null},"fields":{"summary":"Villagers' iron golem detection range is increased for villagers 